---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
import { business } from '../data/site';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'About',href:'/about/'}];
---
<BaseLayout title="About Talon Expeditions | Group Travel Planning Company" description="Talon Expeditions is a U.S.-based group travel planning company for private groups, clubs, communities, businesses, and active or experience-led trips worldwide." image={images.heroAlt} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.heroAlt}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">About Talon Expeditions</p><h1 class="section-title">A group travel company built around the people doing the traveling.</h1><p>{business.description}</p></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell definition-grid"><div class="definition-sticky"><p class="eyebrow">Who we are</p><h2>Group-first travel planning for active, cultural, and experience-led journeys.</h2></div><div class="definition-body"><div class="answer-panel"><h2>What is Talon Expeditions?</h2><p>Talon Expeditions is a U.S.-based travel brand operated by Talon Global LLC. We help private groups, clubs, communities, businesses, and organizers design and coordinate supported trips worldwide, with particular strength in active travel, trekking, learn-to programs, culture, cruises, and group journeys built around a shared interest.</p></div><p>The company exists because group travel becomes complicated in ways that ordinary booking tools do not solve very well. A group does not only need a hotel and a flight. It needs a trip that fits the people, a workable group size, a clear activity level, suppliers that can handle the itinerary, rooming that makes sense, transport that connects, participant information that arrives at the right time, and an organizer who is not carrying the whole operation alone.</p><p>That is the space Talon Expeditions is designed to occupy. We are not trying to be the largest catalog of prepackaged tours. We are building a travel company that can take a real community, a real objective, and a real set of constraints and turn them into an organized journey.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell split-copy-image"><div class="split-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.group}')`}></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Our story</p><h2 class="section-title">Built from the idea that good travel should be easier to organize without becoming generic.</h2><p class="section-copy">Talon Expeditions grew from a broader Talon ecosystem spanning travel, sports, digital operations, and international work. That background shaped a practical view of travel: the experience matters, but the systems behind it matter too.</p><p class="section-copy">The brand initially leaned more heavily into traditional “adventure travel.” The current direction is broader and more useful. We still plan active and demanding trips, but we also work with beginner-friendly groups, cultural travelers, cruise communities, wellness groups, businesses, and people who want movement and experience without turning the vacation into a test of identity.</p><p class="section-copy">The phrase we use internally is <strong>active rest</strong>: travel that gives people something to do, learn, see, or work toward while still leaving room to enjoy being away.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="shell mission-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Mission & vision</p><h2 class="section-title">Make ambitious group travel feel more achievable and more organized.</h2><p style="color:#aaa">The mission is operational before it is inspirational. Better planning should help more people say yes to trips that would otherwise feel too complicated to organize.</p></div><div class="mission-stack"><div class="mission-card"><h3>Mission</h3><p>Help groups create active, experience-led journeys with clearer planning, stronger organizer support, realistic traveler preparation, and destination-specific coordination.</p></div><div class="mission-card"><h3>Vision</h3><p>Build a travel company that can support communities from the first trip idea through repeat programs, skill progression, recurring club travel, and deeper destination experiences over time.</p></div><div class="mission-card"><h3>Operating principle</h3><p>The difficult parts should become more organized as the trip develops. Travelers should arrive understanding what they are doing, what they need, and who is supporting them.</p></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">What we believe</p><h2 class="section-title">Travel can be personal without being improvised.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">These principles guide how we think about trip design, suppliers, organizer relationships, and the traveler experience.</p></div><div class="why-grid"><div class="why-item"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Clarity beats hype</h3><p>Describe the real trip, the real difficulty, the real inclusions, and the real decisions people need to make.</p></div><div class="why-item"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Local knowledge matters</h3><p>Use destination and activity specialists where their knowledge, qualifications, and operational capability add real value.</p></div><div class="why-item"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Groups are not averages</h3><p>Age, fitness, skill, budget, social dynamics, and travel experience can vary significantly inside one community.</p></div><div class="why-item"><span class="number">04</span><h3>Preparation is part of travel</h3><p>Documents, equipment, fitness, rooming, arrivals, and expectations should not be left until the last week.</p></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="feature-band" style={`background-image:url('${images.wildlife}')`}><div class="shell"><div class="band-copy"><p class="eyebrow">What we plan</p><h2 class="section-title">A broad range of trip styles, with a deliberately narrower operating idea.</h2><p>We may plan trekking, diving, cultural journeys, cruises, wildlife travel, learn-to trips, wellness departures, group city travel, or other formats. The common thread is not a single activity. It is supported travel built around a specific group, a specific reason to go, and a practical planning relationship.</p><div class="chip-row"><span class="chip" style="border-color:#68605a">Private groups</span><span class="chip" style="border-color:#68605a">Trekking</span><span class="chip" style="border-color:#68605a">Learn-to travel</span><span class="chip" style="border-color:#68605a">Culture & cruise</span><span class="chip" style="border-color:#68605a">Wildlife</span><span class="chip" style="border-color:#68605a">Active rest</span></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Travel-industry infrastructure</p><h2 class="section-title">Professional systems behind a flexible trip.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Talon Expeditions operates as {business.legalName} and uses travel-industry credentials, supplier relationships, and destination partners appropriate to the trip. Specific supplier relationships are disclosed where relevant and publishable.</p></div><div class="credentials"><div class="credential"><strong>CLIA</strong><span>Cruise-industry infrastructure</span></div><div class="credential"><strong>IATA</strong><span>Air-travel industry infrastructure</span></div><div class="credential"><strong>ARC</strong><span>U.S. travel-industry infrastructure</span></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell split-copy-image"><div><p class="eyebrow">Talon Expeditions and Talon Travel</p><h2 class="section-title">Related travel brands with different jobs.</h2><p class="section-copy">Talon Expeditions is the group-first, active, specialist, and experience-led side of the travel business. Talon Travel is the broader conventional travel brand within the Talon ecosystem. Keeping those roles distinct helps travelers understand which team and operating model fit the trip.</p><p class="section-copy">A complex private trek, learn-to program, hosted community departure, or active cultural journey belongs naturally with Talon Expeditions. A more conventional leisure-travel need may be better suited to Talon Travel as that brand develops.</p><a class="button" href="/why-talon/">Why Groups Choose Talon</a></div><div class="split-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.boat}')`}></div></div></section>
  <PlanningCTA title="The company is built around a simple question: what would make this group trip actually work?" />
</BaseLayout>
